{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/7072-changing-perspective-tomb-thieves-as-player-characters","id":7072,"title":"Changing perspective: Tomb Thieves as Player Characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-09T15:57:10-08:00","id":7072,"title":"Changing perspective: Tomb Thieves as Player Characters","content":"I'm starting this topic for a personal reason, but I hope it will grow into a larger discussion.<br /> <br /> Here's the fact: I'm about to start a sandbox-style game which can be best described as &quot;World of Darkness meets the Arabian Nights&quot;. The PCs are regular humans with the addition of the Dark Heroes template from <b>Mirrors </b>which, relatively speaking, make them quite a bit stronger. I plan to use rules and antagonists taken from pretty much all the gamelines, but Mummy and Mage are probably going to influence the game more than the others. Relics and wonders are a stable of the genre, so it's a given. I'll be sure to warn the characters in game about the danger posed by Mummies and the remnants of the Nameless Empire but, since PCs tend to be greedy when it comes to magical artifacts (and players are even greedier), I've been pondering about the possible outcome of a Mummy's tomb defilement.<br /> <br /> The players have any chance to escape an enraged Arisen? What's the best thing they can do to save themselves? Is it even possible for them to defeat a Mummy?<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, if the thieves are mere mortals with no supernatural patron, losing a Relic is just a nuisance that <i>will </i>be solved quickly or things are more complex than that? I ask because I'm still a newbie when it comes to Mummy and I'm having difficulties to asses the Arisen's power level and limitations, especially on a longer term.<br /> <br /> Any other considerations you think are important when it comes to mortal PCs, mummies and relics?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-09-2013, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T02:45:34-08:00","id":7254,"title":"","content":"How do you escape an undead, unkillable super being who doesn't need to sleep or eat, and has a one track mind when it comes to its property (which is probably very sentimental to him/her)? My advice? RUN! Run away and don't ever look back! And prey to whatever god you believe in that you're somehow faster. Because it can always track you no matter what. Even if you somehow put it down, it will just come back more pissed off than before. And it has an army of worshippers who are also out for your blood and a blind devotion to their god.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you can give them som sort of mcguffin like a flying carpet or a genie that can at least give them a slim chance of surviving. But just a slim one. Those things can shoot metors from the sky.<br /> <br /> Good Luck!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:25:49-08:00","id":7564,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's more or less what I thought; thanks for confirming it. I couldn't have said that better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I guess the best thing I can do is to wait until the PCs gain a lot of experience, spread terror of mummies through cautionary tales whispered in the dark corners of bazaars and be <i>extremely </i>careful before even allowing them to meet an Arisen. I'll limit myself to Cults, non-Iremite relics and the occasional Shuankhsen for now.<br /> <br /> The best thing the players can do, of course, is to not mess with a Mummy and avoid to steal her stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-10-2013, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T16:50:56-08:00","id":7725,"title":"","content":"i'd say a shuanksen is definately a good way to introduce mortals to the mummy themes, especially as they are weaker and more destructive. it is possible for the pcs to awaken a mummy and escape it. theyd then have to face the cultists, and be on the move to escape the mummy. its possible, though exhausting, to stay a step ahead of the mummy until it descends or is faced with more pressing matters. during this time, itd be wise for the relic hunters to research the cult, and maybe discover some hard facts about the mummy and its activities. a unique approach would be to learn enough of the mummy's past to use as a bargaining chip--spare our lives and take back your relic, and we will help you (though the mummy may not remember what the humans are talking about, it might be interested in finding out what the humans know). in return, reward us.. of course, at low enough level of descent, the mummy can be destroyed, but it wont be immediately obvious to the pcs that the mummy grows weaker over time. instead they may assume that the mummy is an unkillable demigod. this is good for using the horror element of mummy, and excite the players when they are faced with the mummy and do indeed destroy it. except, of course, that it will return. the mummy always returns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T13:54:13-08:00","id":18692,"title":"","content":"I'm actually running a game like this. Hunter, technically, with two Aegis Kai Doru, an Ashwood Abbey and a ghoul.<br /> <br /> They haven't gotten to the Mummy yet (I have two in the city) but they're getting close. So I hope you keep us updated on how your game goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T10:38:00-08:00","id":19257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/7072-changing-perspective-tomb-thieves-as-player-characters?p=18692#post18692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually running a game like this. Hunter, technically, with two Aegis Kai Doru, an Ashwood Abbey and a ghoul.<br /> <br /> They haven't gotten to the Mummy yet (I have two in the city) but they're getting close. So I hope you keep us updated on how your game goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect it to happen quickly but, as soon as they face a Mummy, I'll tell you how things went. I hope you'll keep us informed us about your game as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-27-2013, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T08:05:02-08:00","id":19739,"title":"","content":"Well another way to handle this is by making the Mummy spare the Lives of the Intruders, in Exchange for Servitude. Slowly the Characters gain Power and finally they must find a Way to overthrow their Mummy-Master before he discards them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}